  "body": "From https://github.com/validator/validator/issues/310\n\nI had noted in https://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/1356#issuecomment-222829115 that this was a new parse error, but somehow missed that this is commonly used syntax in IE conditional comments.\n\nI think we should allow `<!--<!-->`, but not allow `<!--<!--->` or `<!--<!---->` etc. So one more state I believe. 😐\n\n(Also change syntax section to allow comment data ending with `<!` (but still disallow `<!-`).)\n\nAck @eel-in-a-hovercraft\ncc @sideshowbarker \n\nPrevious issue/pr that caused this:\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/issues/1351\nhttps://github.com/whatwg/html/pull/1356\n",
